60
00:04:15,748 --> 00:04:21,209
LLM 默认如何组织观点，以及你可以在大纲里调整哪些地方。
how LLMs tend to organize ideas by default and what you can adjust in your outlines,

61
00:04:21,209 --> 00:04:25,968
段落和过渡，让文章不再读起来像 AI 模板
Paragraphs and transitions so a piece stops reading like an AI template

62
00:04:25,968 --> 00:04:28,620
甚至在你动单个用词之前。
Before you even touch individual words.

63
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:33,457
当人们说“这读起来像 ChatGPT”时，他们往往是对结构有反应，
When people say this sounds like ChatGPT, they are often reacting to structure,

64
00:04:33,457 --> 00:04:34,960
而不只是用词选择。
not just the choice of words.

65
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,526
单看句子本身没问题，
The sentences look fine on their own,

66
00:04:37,526 --> 00:04:41,280
但它们的排列方式让人感觉套路化、过于熟悉。
but the way they are arranged feels generic and overfamiliar.

67
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:47,259
有些地方不对劲。最常见的结构模式包括几类我们
There's something off. The most common structural patterns include a few things we

68
