很容易发现的情况，比如大量使用项目符号列表，
can easily spot, like a heavy use of bullet lists,

69
00:04:50,574 --> 00:04:54,455
很多相似的小标题，其实意思都差不多，
many similar subheadings that all mean the same,

70
00:04:54,455 --> 00:04:56,800
还有某种标准作文框架。
some kind of standard essay frame.

71
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:59,665
一个泛泛的开头，先说明主题，
A general intro that announces the topic,

72
00:04:59,665 --> 00:05:02,596
三个主体段落反复呼应这个句子，
three body sections that mirror that sentence,

73
00:05:02,596 --> 00:05:06,260
然后一个总结段复述每个小标题，而且非常空泛。
then a recap that restates each heading and is very general.

74
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:12,582
另一个危险信号是全文段落长度都差不多，或者一直在写文章本身
Another red flag is same-sized paragraphs throughout or writing about the article

75
00:05:12,582 --> 00:05:17,440
而不是写主题本身，比如“在本节中，我们将首先了解”，
itself instead of the topic, like "in this section, we'll look at first,"

76
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:20,240
“我们将分析，然后我们将探讨”等等。
"we'll examine, then we'll explore, etc."

77
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:25,520
还有很多泛泛而谈、过度简化的例子。我很讨厌这些。
There are also a lot of generic, oversimplified examples. I really hate those.

78
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:27,985
它们对文章没有任何增色。
They don't add anything to the article.

79
00:05:27,985 --> 00:05:31,680
而且它们通常用来解释本来就已经很简单的东西。
And usually they are used to explain something that is already quite simple.

80
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:36,124
而生成的文章通常有一个非常套路化的开头
And generated articles usually have a super generic introduction

81
00:05:36,124 --> 00:05:39,109
和结尾，比如最后一段
and conclusion at the end, like a final paragraph

82
00:05:39,109 --> 00:05:43,915
会拉高到一个安全但空泛的概括，不加任何具体内容。
that zooms out to a safe high-level statement without adding anything specific

83
00:05:43,915 --> 00:05:48,865
单独来看，这些大多没问题。大多数情况下，它们对学生作文、
Individually, these are fine. For the most part, they are useful for school essays,

84
00:05:48,865 --> 00:05:52,360
文档和 how-to 博客里都很有用。问题是当
documentation and how-to blogs. The problem is that when

85
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:56,040
它们都按同样的顺序一起出现，而不管主题是什么。
All of them show up together in the same order, no matter the topic.

86
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:00,614
到那时，文章就不再感觉像是有人真的在写，
At that point, the piece stops feeling like someone's actually

87
00:06:00,614 --> 00:06:04,400
而是开始像一个被反复使用，甚至可以说被滥用的框架。
and starts feeling like a reused, not to say overused frame.

88
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:09,970
大语言模型会陷入这种情况，是因为它们的训练数据里充满了那种模式：教科书、
LLMs fall into this because their training data is full of that pattern, textbooks,

89
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:13,145
教程、企业解释文章、学生作文，
tutorials, corporate explainers, student essays,

90
00:06:13,145 --> 00:06:17,473
所有它们能接触到的东西。当你要求“写一篇关于 X 的文章”时，
everything they can get their hands on when you ask, write an article about X,

91
00:06:17,473 --> 00:06:20,720
模型并不是在追求有意思的结构。
The model isn't optimizing for an interesting shape.

92
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:25,831
它是在寻找安全的文章结构，然后把你的话题塞进去。
It's reaching for safe article structure and slotting your topic into it

93
00:06:25,831 --> 00:06:29,769
如果你想保留 AI 的速度，又不想要那种模板感，
If you want to keep the speed of AI without that template feel,

94
00:06:29,769 --> 00:06:31,700
你就必须改变这个层面。
you have to change this level.

95
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:36,180
第一，大纲、段落形状和过渡。
First, the outline, the paragraph's shape and transitions.

96
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:40,625
一个有用的规则是：文章结构完全由你自己把控，
A helpful rule is to fully own the structure of the article

97
00:06:40,625 --> 00:06:42,220
然后让模型来填充内容。
and let the model fill it.

98
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:46,920
基本上就是让模型做苦力活，但思考仍由你自己保留。
Basically let the model do the hard work, but you still keep the thinking.

99
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:50,860
我有几个实用的方法可以帮你改变这一点。第一，
I have a few practical ways to help you change that. First,

100
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:52,600
自己先确定大纲。
decide the outline yourself.

101
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:57,802
在写提示词之前或写提示词的过程中，自己快速列一个大纲，
Before you prompt or during your prompt, sketch a quick outline yourself,

102
00:06:57,802 --> 00:07:01,720
从哪里开始，哪些部分最重要，以及在哪里结束。
where to start, which sections matter most, and where to end.

103
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:07,440
让一些部分短一些，另一些长一些。它们不需要对称。
Let some sections be short and others longer. They don't need to be symmetrical.

104
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:12,036
然后让模型做类似“把这个大纲展开成正文”的事。
Then ask the model for something like, turn this outline into prose.

105
00:07:12,036 --> 00:07:15,070
不要在这里已有的内容之外加开头或结尾。
Don't add intro or conclusion beyond what's here.

106
00:07:15,470 --> 00:07:18,190
不要额外创建小标题。这一点很重要。
Don't create extra subheadings. This one is important.

107
00:07:18,630 --> 00:07:22,796
你是在告诉它留在你的框架内，而不是发明它自己的框架，
You are telling it to stay inside your frame instead of inventing its own

108
00:07:22,796 --> 00:07:25,990
也不是去复制它在互联网上看到的东西。
and basically copying what it has seen on the internet.

109
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:29,510
第二，优先使用段落而不是列表，尤其是
Second, favor paragraphs over lists, especially

110
00:07:29,510 --> 00:07:32,720
如果你在写一篇适合阅读的文章。
if you're trying to create a nice reading piece.

111
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:35,869
大语言模型会过度使用项目符号和小标题，
LLMs overuse bullet points and headings,

112
00:07:35,869 --> 00:07:39,160
因为很多在线内容就是这样结构的。
because that's how a lot of online content is structured.

113
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:44,846
如果你想要读起来更像文章，而不是像幻灯片演示稿，
If you want something that reads more like an article and less like a slide deck,

114
00:07:44,846 --> 00:07:45,840
你就必须明确说出来。
you have to say.

115
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:52,214
所以你可以加一个简单的限制，比如主要用完整句子来写，
So you can add a simple constraint like, write primarily in complete sentences

116
00:07:52,214 --> 00:07:54,960
并使用结构良好的段落。
and well-structured paragraphs.

117
00:07:55,580 --> 00:08:01,356
除非内容确实需要，否则避免使用列表或项目符号。例如，
Avoid lists or bullet points unless the content clearly needs them. For example,

118
00:08:01,356 --> 00:08:03,820
具体步骤或不同的条目。
specific steps or distinct items.

119
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:09,787
小标题要少用，只用于明显不同的部分，
Use subheadings sparingly, only for clearly different sections,

120
00:08:09,787 --> 00:08:11,540
不要每个新想法都加。
not for every new idea.

121
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:16,666
这会把模型推向连续叙述、更完整的段落，
This pushes the model towards continuous narrative, fuller paragraphs,

122
00:08:16,666 --> 00:08:20,170
更顺滑的过渡，以及更少的列表式碎片。
smoother transitions, and fewer list-shaped fragments.

123
00:08:20,530 --> 00:08:23,972
你随时可以把其中一部分改成列表
You can always turn part of it into a list later

124
00:08:23,972 --> 00:08:29,770
如果你真的需要。第三，限制类比，别让它们承担文章结构。
if you genuinely need. Third, limit analogies so they don't carry the structure.

125
00:08:30,410 --> 00:08:35,130
模型也喜欢靠类比来让自己显得更有吸引力。
Models also like to lean on analogies as an easy way to sound engaging.

126
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:40,090
类比太多或太弱，会让文章显得注水、含糊。
Too many of them or weak ones make the piece feel padded and blurry.

127
00:08:40,710 --> 00:08:43,950
一个糟糕的类比远比完全没有类比更糟。
A bad analogy is way worse than no analogy at all.

128
00:08:44,470 --> 00:08:48,582
你可以用一条像这样的简短规则控制它们
You can keep them under control with a short rule like this one

129
00:08:48,582 --> 00:08:53,016
让结构锚定在实际论点上，
that should keep the structure anchored in the actual argument,

130
00:08:53,016 --> 00:08:54,790
而不是靠一串比喻。
not a string of metaphors.

131
00:08:55,190 --> 00:08:57,150
那些模型在其他文章里见惯的比喻。
that the model has seen in other articles.

132
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:02,840
第四，在提示词里减少元话术和指路语，把它们限制在对应小节里。
Fourth, reduce meta and signposting in the prompt. Cap them in the section.

133
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:06,462
我们会从这条开始：当你审阅草稿时，
We'll start with this one when you review the draft,

134
00:09:06,462 --> 00:09:11,079
做一轮只针对元话术的快速检查并删除，删掉清嗓子式的开头，
do a fast pass just for meta and delete cut throat-clearing openings,

135
00:09:11,079 --> 00:09:15,297
删除重复小标题的总结句，以及任何结尾段
recap sentences that repeat headings and any final paragraphs

136
00:09:15,297 --> 00:09:18,720
只是把读者已经知道的内容换种说法再说一遍。
that only rephrase what the reader already knows.

137
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:24,368
第五，打破对称。让模型变化段落长度。例如，
Fifth, break the symmetry. Tell the model to vary paragraph length. For example,

138
00:09:24,368 --> 00:09:27,340
有些小节可以很短，有些则可以写得更深入。
some sections can be short, others can go deeper.

139
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:30,897
不要在每个小节结尾都加迷你总结。
Don't end every section with a mini summary

140
00:09:30,897 --> 00:09:35,399
如果草稿仍有 3 个长度相等、标题相似的小节，
if the draft still has 3 equal sections with similar headings,

141
00:09:35,399 --> 00:09:38,602
就手动修掉：合并重叠的部分，
fix that manually, merge overlapping parts,

142
00:09:38,602 --> 00:09:42,065
把较弱的小标题降成普通段落，
demote weaker headings into plain paragraphs,

143
00:09:42,065 --> 00:09:44,403
或者直接删掉一整节。只要
or cut a section entirely as soon

144
00:09:44,403 --> 00:09:48,559
大纲不再像标准三段式的文章，
as the outline stops looking like a near three-part essay,

145
00:09:48,559 --> 00:09:53,840
文章读起来就不那么像默认的 AI 输出了。第六，用 AI 来搭建
the piece reads less like a default AI output. Sixth, use AI for building.

146
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,920
积木，而不是完成整个小节。
Blocks, not finished sections.

147
00:09:56,600 --> 00:10:01,437
与其让它“写第 2 节”，不如用模型生成组件，比如：“给我三种
Instead of "write section 2," use the model to generate components like give me three

148
00:10:01,437 --> 00:10:03,960
组织这一节的不同方式。”
different ways to structure this section.

149
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:08,940
列出能让这个论点变得更具体的例子，或者更好的做法：
List specific examples that would make this argument concrete or even better.

150
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:12,249
我想和攀岩领域做一个类比，
I want to make an analogy with the climbing world,

151
00:10:12,249 --> 00:10:15,300
因为我觉得这能帮读者把点连起来。
as I think it would help the reader connect the dots.

152
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:17,900
帮我想一个适合这里的类比。”
Help me come up with one that fits here.

153
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:21,620
我最近刚用过这个方法，效果出奇地好。
I just recently used that one and it was surprisingly good.

154
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:26,363
另一个用法是让它为这些段落建议两个过渡句，
Another one could be to suggest two transitions between these paragraphs

155
00:10:26,363 --> 00:10:28,320
而且不要复述我们刚读过的内容。
that don't recap what we just read.

156
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:33,167
然后你来做选择、重排和衔接。模型给你素材，
You then choose, reorder, and connect. The model gives you the material.

157
00:10:33,167 --> 00:10:35,880
你决定它如何流动、是否相关。
You decide how it flows and if it's relevant.

158
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:40,200
第七，先做结构检查，再做语言润色。
Seventh, do a structural pass before a language pass

159
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:43,000
在你真正动手改句子之前。
before you actually touch the sentences.

160
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:45,760
把每一段变成一行总结。
Turn each paragraph into a one-line summary.

161
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:51,120
把这些总结当成大纲来读。然后问自己几个问题。
Read those lines as if they were an outline. Then just ask yourself some questions.

162
00:10:51,630 --> 00:10:54,630
它读起来像你，还是像一篇套路化的博客文章？
Does it sound like you or like a generic blog post?

163
00:10:54,990 --> 00:10:58,008
如果是后者，就重排、删减或收紧
If it's the latter, reorder, cut or tighten

164
00:10:58,008 --> 00:11:03,038
直到顺序和你亲口解释这个主题的方式一致。
until the sequence matches how you'd like to explain the topic out loud,

165
00:11:03,038 --> 00:11:05,637
通常删掉第一段、
often removing the first paragraph,

166
00:11:05,637 --> 00:11:11,590
修剪复述并提前一步结尾，就足以去掉大部分 AI 感。
trimming the recap and ending one step earlier is enough to remove most of the AI feel.

167
00:11:12,650 --> 00:11:17,284
一旦结构是你自己的，草稿就已经不那么像模型写的了，
Once the structure is yours, the draft already feels less like a model,

168
00:11:17,284 --> 00:11:19,090
即使它最初是 AI 生成的。
even if it was AI generated.

169
00:11:19,770 --> 00:11:24,826
之后，你可以专注于语言本身：建立你自己的 AI 词汇清单、
After that, you can focus on language: building your own list of AI words,

170
00:11:24,826 --> 00:11:28,450
收紧措辞，并使用反 AI 垃圾文本提示词。
tightening phrasing, and using an anti-slop prompt.

171
00:11:28,690 --> 00:11:32,770
让模型从一开始就不再反复使用同样的词汇。
So the model stops reaching for the same vocabulary in the first place.

172
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:38,875
这些做好之后，AI 感主要来自句子层面的习惯：重复、
Once this all works, the AI feel comes from sentence-level habits: repetition,

173
00:11:38,875 --> 00:11:43,401
套路化的开头和结尾、模糊的形容词、过于礼貌的语气
generic openings and endings, vague adjectives, overly polite tone

174
00:11:43,401 --> 00:11:45,580
以及反复出现的一组 AI 词汇。
and a recurring set of AI words.

175
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:49,180
你可以把这些变成提示词里的明确规则。
You can turn these into explicit rules in your prompt.

176
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:53,540
这样第一稿就能避开大部分问题，我们稍后会加入这些规则。
So the first draft already avoids most of them, which we will do shortly.

177
00:11:54,030 --> 00:11:57,190
但先让我们逐条看看它们，以及可以怎么修。
But let's see each of them and what we can do to fix them.

178
00:11:58,030 --> 00:12:02,394
第一，重复。AI 文本一个常见迹象是看似无害的重复，
First, we have repetition. A common sign of AI is harmless-looking

179
00:12:02,394 --> 00:12:05,280
这种重复会让文本显得机械。
repetition that makes the text feel mechanical.

180
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:11,480
好几个句子或段落以同样的方式开头，或一遍遍使用同样的节奏。
Several sentences or paragraphs starting the same way or using the same rhythm again and again.

181
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:14,360
所以这里有一条提示词规则，你可以在这种情况下使用。
So here's a prompt rule you can use in that case.

182
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,685
顺便说一句，我会再重复一遍，
By the way, I will repeat that,

183
00:12:16,685 --> 00:12:21,051
但我在视频里分享的所有提示词，都可以在文章版本里找到，就在下方描述区的第一个
but all the prompts I'm sharing in the video are in the article version in the first

184
00:12:21,051 --> 00:12:22,720
链接里。
link in the description below.

185
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:28,543
然后，在发送那条提示词之后，有一轮编辑是只读开头部分，
Then after sending that prompt, an edit pass would be to read once just for openings,

186
00:12:28,543 --> 00:12:33,050
忽略意思，只看每句话开头的几个词。
ignore the meaning, and look only at the first few words of each sentence.

187
00:12:33,650 --> 00:12:38,764
只要看到同一个开头或句式出现三次，就删掉或合并，
Wherever you see the same opener or pattern three times, cut or combine,

188
00:12:38,764 --> 00:12:44,730
通常两句模型生成的句子可以合并成一句更清晰的话，同时不丢失内容。
often two model sentences can become one clearer sentence without losing content.

189
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:49,870
接下来是开头和结尾。这是 LLM 的一个大问题。
Then we have openings and endings. A big issue with LLMs.

190
00:12:50,470 --> 00:12:53,896
套路化的开头和结论是一个很明显的破绽。
Generic introductions and conclusions are a clear tell.

191
00:12:53,896 --> 00:12:57,750
它们会先宣布文章要讲什么，最后再重复一遍。
They announce what the piece will do and then repeat it at the end.

192
00:12:58,350 --> 00:13:02,710
所以这里有一条提示词规则，可以在内容生成后缓解这个问题。
So here's a prompt rule to mitigate that once it generates the content.

193
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:07,299
如果第一段只需要稍微改改就能用在另一篇文章里，
If the first paragraph could be used on a different article with minor changes,

194
00:13:07,299 --> 00:13:08,670
就删掉它，然后重写。
cut it out and rewrite it.

195
00:13:09,110 --> 00:13:12,944
如果最后一段只是重复读者已经知道的内容，
If the last paragraph only repeats what the reader already knows,

196
00:13:12,944 --> 00:13:16,430
就删掉它，或者换成一句具体的结尾句。
delete it or replace it with one specific closing sentence.

197
00:13:17,150 --> 00:13:18,270
现在来说形容词。
Now, the adjectives.

198
00:13:19,110 --> 00:13:24,278
模型经常依赖积极但模糊的形容词，比如 robust（稳健）、seamless（无缝）、
Models often rely on positive but vague adjectives like robust, seamless,

199
00:13:24,278 --> 00:13:30,840
groundbreaking（突破性）、transformative（变革性）、pivotal（关键）、intriguing（引人入胜）、innovative（创新）、comprehensive（全面）、safe（安全）等。
groundbreaking, transformative, pivotal, intriguing, innovative, comprehensive, safe, etc.

200
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:36,120
它们听起来很有信心，但并没有增加信息。所以这里有一条对应的提示词规则。
They sound confident, but don't add information. So here's the prompt rule for that.

201
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:42,429
内容生成后，拿一段出来，把所有形容词都去掉，
Once the content is generated, take one paragraph and strip it out of all adjectives,

202
00:13:42,429 --> 00:13:46,640
然后只把那些能真正改变含义的形容词放回去。
then only put back the ones that change meaning in a useful way.

203
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,800
用具体细节替代模糊表达。
Replace vague with details.

204
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,246
比如 “Robust system” 可以改成 “service”
Robust system can become service

205
00:13:51,246 --> 00:13:54,960
能每秒处理 10,000 个请求且不丢失数据。
that handles 10,000 requests per second without dropping data.

206
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:58,190
不管怎样，形容词都有点没用，
In any case, adjectives are a bit useless

207
00:13:58,190 --> 00:14:01,910
你通常需要在真正重要的细节上做到精确。
and you usually want to be precise on the details that matter.

208
00:14:02,870 --> 00:14:05,489
现在来说模型那种经典的礼貌腔，
Now, the classical politeness of models,

209
00:14:05,489 --> 00:14:08,931
因为模型被训练得要安全、不得罪人，
because models are trained to be safe and inoffensive,

210
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:11,550
所以它们默认会非常礼貌和正式。
they default to be very polite and formal.

211
00:14:12,110 --> 00:14:17,390
比如 “I hope this email finds you well. I would like to take a moment to” 等等。
Like, I hope this email finds you well. I would like to take a moment to etc.

212
00:14:17,830 --> 00:14:23,810
或者 “I humbly request” 之类。你可以用这条提示词规则来尽量缓解这个问题。
Or I humbly request etc. You can use this prompt rule to try to mitigate this a bit.

213
00:14:24,410 --> 00:14:29,410
然后问问自己，这些话你会不会真的说出口。如果不会，就压缩到你能自然说出来的程度。
Then ask yourself if you would say this out loud. If not, tighten it until you can.

214
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:36,043
比如 “I wanted to kindly follow up regarding” 这类表达，通常只需要变成
So something like I wanted to kindly follow up regarding etc usually becomes just

215
00:14:36,043 --> 00:14:38,810
“checking in on” 或者 “any updates on” 这类。
checking in on or any updates on etc.

216
00:14:39,650 --> 00:14:43,770
基本上，如果你把它说出口，而且感觉自然，那就是可以用的版本。
Basically if you say it out loud and you feel right, it's the good one to go with.

217
00:14:44,370 --> 00:14:47,370
关键的一点。现在来看我们的词汇黑名单。
Crucially. Now, let's see our words blacklist.

218
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:53,630
有些词和短语现在读起来就像标准 AI 输出，比如 delve、realm、
Some words and phrases now read as standard AI output like delve, realm,

219
00:14:53,630 --> 00:14:59,290
ever evolving landscape、imagine、embark on a journey、navigate 等等。
ever evolving landscape, imagine, embark on a journey, navigate, etc.

220
00:15:00,330 --> 00:15:03,730
并不存在一份通用清单。不同领域有不同的习惯性用词。
There is no universal list. Different fields have different tics.

221
00:15:04,010 --> 00:15:07,204
但你可以维护一份简短的清单，列出你不想看到的词，
But keep a small list of words you don't want to see

222
00:15:07,204 --> 00:15:09,930
除非是你刻意选择使用它们。
unless you've chosen them deliberately.

223
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:11,450
我们这里确实有一份清单。
We do have a list here.

224
00:15:11,450 --> 00:15:13,290
当然，就我们自己的情况来说，
We use, in our case, of course,

225
00:15:13,290 --> 00:15:17,634
我们会随着时间更新这份清单，因为新模型会出现新的模式，
update this list over time because new patterns appear with new models

226
00:15:17,634 --> 00:15:20,210
而它们肯定会来烦你。
and they will definitely come bother you.

227
00:15:20,810 --> 00:15:23,530
接下来，解决忠实度和确定性的问题。
Then let's fix fidelity and certainty.

228
00:15:23,890 --> 00:15:28,459
当模型根据笔记、转录稿或来源文章来工作时，
When the model is working from notes, a transcript or a source article,

229
00:15:28,459 --> 00:15:29,930
它需要明确的限制。
it needs clear limits.

230
00:15:30,450 --> 00:15:32,010
这是我们在这种情况下使用的一条提示词。
Here's a prompt we use for that.

231
00:15:32,530 --> 00:15:37,890
接下来，你要在语气和视角上保持一致，同时避免效果下降。
Next, you want consistency without performance drop through tone and point of view.

232
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:43,989
这里有一条提示词正好能做到这一点。最后，要优化直接性、
Here's a prompt that achieves exactly that. And finally, optimize for directness,

233
00:15:43,989 --> 00:15:45,680
清晰性和简洁性。
clarity and conciseness.

234
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:51,240
修辞性钩子和重复定义是低质 AI 文本重新冒出来的常见方式。
Rhetorical hooks and repeated definitions are a common way AI slop creeps back in.

235
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:53,440
这里有一条提示词可以帮助解决这个问题。
Here's a prompt to help with that.

236
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:54,440
顺便说一下。
By the way.

237
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:56,757
你可以找到一条非常详细的提示词
You can find a super detailed prompt

238
00:15:56,757 --> 00:16:02,200
以及我们刚讲到的所有内容的完整版本，就在下方描述区链接的文章里。
and a complete version of all we just saw in the article linked in the description below.

239
00:16:02,710 --> 00:16:06,110
所以请直接去复制、粘贴，并在你的工作中使用它。
So please go ahead, copy, paste and use it in your work.

240
00:16:06,310 --> 00:16:10,101
这个模块可以放在你更大的通用模板里，和任务、
This block can sit inside your larger universal template with task,

241
00:16:10,101 --> 00:16:12,030
受众、结构和准确性。
audience structure and accuracy.

242
00:16:12,470 --> 00:16:15,383
对于邮件，你可能想保留礼貌用语那几行。
For emails, you might want to keep the politeness rows

243
00:16:15,383 --> 00:16:17,584
剩下的可以删掉；对于长文文章，
and trim the rest for long-form articles,

244
00:16:17,584 --> 00:16:22,310
你可能会保留全部，并用你所在领域的套话扩充黑名单。
you might keep everything and extend the blacklist with your domain-specific clichés.

245
00:16:23,110 --> 00:16:25,870
重点是，你不再需要每次重新来一遍。
The main point is that you no longer have to reinvent.

246
00:16:26,430 --> 00:16:30,203
不要每次都让它像 ChatGPT 那样说话；你一旦决定了
Please don't sound like ChatGPT every time you decide once,

247
00:16:30,203 --> 00:16:32,240
你希望语言如何表现，
how you want language to behave.

248
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:35,440
模型就会把这一点当作它工作职责的一部分。
And the model reads that as part of its job description.

249
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:40,922
遗憾的是，即使有好的结构和像这样仔细的提示词，
Unfortunately, even with a good structure and a careful prompt like this one,

250
00:16:40,922 --> 00:16:44,320
大多数模型第一次也不会完全遵守每一条规则。
most models will not follow every rule on the first try.

251
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:47,949
它们仍会偷偷塞进“快节奏世界”这类套话，
They will still sneak in a fast-paced world,

252
00:16:47,949 --> 00:16:53,760
同一个过渡词用三次，或者又滑回作文式的结论。
reuse the same transition three times or drift back into an essay-style conclusion.

253
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:57,800
这很正常。目标不是一次性得到完美初稿。
That's normal. The goal is not to get a perfect one-shot draft.

254
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:02,024
而是建立一个循环，让模型完成大部分清理工作，
It's to set up a loop where the model does most of the cleanup

255
00:17:02,024 --> 00:17:04,600
在你投入大量编辑时间之前。
before you spend serious editing time.

256
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:09,628
一个有用的思考方式是：第一次回复是版本 0，
A useful way to think about this is the first response is version 0,

257
00:17:09,628 --> 00:17:11,640
不是你只能硬着头皮用下去的初稿。
not a draft you are stuck with.

258
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:16,985
你先用完整模板来提示内容和结构，
You start by prompting for content and structure using your full template,

259
00:17:16,985 --> 00:17:20,600
包括任务、受众、大纲，以及你的反 AI 垃圾文本语言规则。
task, audience, outline, and your anti-slop language rules.

260
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,960
版本 0 应该有正确的想法和大致正确的顺序。
Version 0 should have the right ideas and roughly the correct order.

261
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:27,800
如果结构不对，你先修结构。
If the structure is wrong, you fix that first.

262
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:32,480
在那些你打算删掉或移动的部分上润色语言没有意义。
There's no point in polishing language on sections you are going to cut or move.

263
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:37,080
一旦结构没问题，你就让一个大语言模型当评审。
Once the structure works, you let an LLM act as a judge.

264
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:41,640
实践中，这通常意味着开第二个对话窗口，或者换一个不同的模型。
In practice, that often means opening a second chat or using a different model.

265
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:46,080
第一个对话窗口是你的写作模型，也就是生成初稿的那个。
The first chat is your writer model, the one that produced the draft.

266
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:51,867
第二个对话窗口或模型是你的编辑模型，它唯一的工作就是找出
